---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import LinkCard from '../../components/LinkCard.astro';

const relatedPages = [
  { title: 'College Football Hub', href: '/college-football-betting', description: 'Complete CFB guide' },
  { title: 'Bowl Games', href: '/college-football/bowl-games', description: 'Postseason betting' },
  { title: 'Conference Championships', href: '/college-football/conference-championships', description: 'Title games' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Rivalry Game Betting Dynamics"
  description="How traditional rivalries affect college football betting, motivation factors, public perception, and market dynamics in rivalry matchups."
>
  <Hero
    title="Rivalry Game Betting Dynamics"
    subtitle="How Traditional Matchups Affect Betting Markets"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            Rivalry games feature heightened emotion, motivation that transcends records, and public betting influenced by fandom rather than analysis. Teams with losing records can play their best game of the year against a hated rival. Markets often account for rivalry intensity, but public bias toward popular programs and narrative-driven betting can still create inefficiencies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="How Do Rivalries Affect Betting?" id="effects">
        <h3>Motivation beyond records</h3>
        <p>
          A 4-7 team playing its rival might perform at a 7-4 level. Rivalry weeks can bring out peak performance regardless of season trajectory.
        </p>

        <h3>Public bias</h3>
        <p>
          Casual bettors often bet on the teams they root for. Rivalry weeks amplify this bias as emotional attachment peaks.
        </p>

        <h3>Coaching focus</h3>
        <p>
          Rivalry games often receive extra preparation time and emphasis. Coaches who otherwise struggle may excel in their rivalry game.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What This Means for Bettors" id="what-means">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Don't trust season records blindly:</strong> Rivalries create motivational equalizers.</li>
          <li><strong>Consider public bias:</strong> Popular teams may be overbet in rivalry situations.</li>
          <li><strong>Look at recent series history:</strong> Some rivalries are lopsided; others are competitive regardless of talent.</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Key Takeaways" id="takeaways">
        <ul>
          <li>Rivalry motivation can transcend season-long performance</li>
          <li>Public bias peaks during rivalry weeks</li>
          <li>Coaching preparation often intensifies for rivals</li>
          <li>Historical series results provide useful context</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Related Resources" id="related">
        <div class="related-grid">
          {relatedPages.map((page) => (
            <LinkCard title={page.title} href={page.href} description={page.description} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0; }
  .quick-take { background-color: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .quick-take h2 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); }
  .quick-take p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--spacing-md); margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .related-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
